From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satyanarayana K V P <satyanarayana.k.v.p@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:24:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/guc: Protect timeout handling from device unplug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The GuC scheduler timeout callback accesses device and GT state while
handling a timed-out job. Guard the callback with drm_dev_enter() and
drm_dev_exit() so device unplug waits for in-flight timeout handling.
If unplug has already started, mark the job with -ENODEV and return it
to the scheduler for cleanup.

Fixes: 6eb2aad402cc ("drm/xe: Move hw_engine_fini to devm managed")
Signed-off-by: Satyanarayana K V P <satyanarayana.k.v.p@intel.com>
Cc: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>
Cc: Piotr Piórkowski <piotr.piorkowski@intel.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Reviewed-by: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261013152417.3189567-7-satyanarayana.k.v.p@intel.com
Signed-off-by: Akanksha Hotta <akanksha.hotta@intel.com>
(cherry-picked from commit 3e9a95f3df5b0f9de163c5ee4e4e287750ef9655 linux-next)
Signed-off-by: Akanksha Hotta <akanksha.hotta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
index ec6b1e6a468b..223b047d3f6e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
@@ -1569,6 +1569,7 @@ guc_exec_queue_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *drm_job)
 	int err = -ETIME;
 	pid_t pid = -1;
 	bool wedged = false, wedge_device = false, skip_timeout_check;
+	int idx;
 
 	xe_gt_assert(guc_to_gt(guc), !exec_queue_destroyed(q));
 
@@ -1584,6 +1585,11 @@ guc_exec_queue_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *drm_job)
 	    vf_recovery(guc))
 		return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
 
+	if (!drm_dev_enter(&xe->drm, &idx)) {
+		xe_sched_job_set_error(job, -ENODEV);
+		return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
+	}
+
 	/* Kill the run_job entry point */
 	if (xe_exec_queue_is_multi_queue(q))
 		xe_guc_exec_queue_group_stop(q);
@@ -1756,6 +1762,7 @@ guc_exec_queue_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *drm_job)
 	 * We want the job added back to the pending list so it gets freed; this
 	 * is what DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG does.
 	 */
+	drm_dev_exit(idx);
 	return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
 
 rearm:
@@ -1769,6 +1776,7 @@ guc_exec_queue_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *drm_job)
 	else
 		xe_sched_submission_start(sched);
 handle_vf_resume:
+	drm_dev_exit(idx);
 	return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
 }
 
